"id":"q-01a309be3ad0","stem":"In the life cycle of malaria parasites, human being is a","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reservoir host in which asexual development of the parasite"},{"label":"B","text":"Paratenic host in which some developmental stages of parasite occurs"},{"label":"C","text":"Intermediate host in which there is sexual development of the parasite"},{"label":"D","text":"Definitive host in which there is asexual development of parasites"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ab1cab14f7bc","stem":"Which statement is true about stable zones for malaria transmission?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The prevalence of infection is persistently high and endemicity is relative insensitive to environmental changes"},{"label":"B","text":"Variation of transmission is minimal over many years"},{"label":"C","text":"Seasonal variation occurs and transmission can occur with very few vectors"},{"label":"D","text":"High level of immunity development within population due to continuous transmission"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":fal