le of the intestinal Amoeba that is most likely to be seen in the permanent stained smear is the","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cyst"},{"label":"B","text":"Precyst"},{"label":"C","text":"Trophozoite"},{"label":"D","text":"Pretrophozoite"},{"label":"E","text":"Metacysts Page 7 of 13"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-23992dd9263b","stem":"If amoebic trophozoites measuring 13um and containing red blood cells within the cytoplasm are seen in permanent stained smear, the correct report would indicate the presence of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Entamoeba coli trophozoites"},{"label":"B","text":"Entamoeba harmatani trophozoites"},{"label":"C","text":"Entamoeba histolytica trophozoites"},{"label":"D","text":"Entamoeba polecki trophozoites"},{"label":"E","text":"Balantidium coli trophozoites"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-77c728538754","stem":"Which of the following infection are more likely to cause major symptoms in the immunocompromised patient","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topic