","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is common in Ethiopian highlands"},{"label":"B","text":"Adults are affected more than the children"},{"label":"C","text":"Mega ureters is not one of the pathologies"},{"label":"D","text":"Aspiration pneumonia can be caused by Mega esophagus Page 12 of 13"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-60265a8893ca","stem":"All of the following is true about diagnosis of chagas disease except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Direct agglutination test with IgM serum fraction is sensitive in acute cases"},{"label":"B","text":"Xeno-diagnosis can be used"},{"label":"C","text":"PCR techniques has no place in diagnosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Microscopy of blood in first month may reveal T.cruzi trypomastigotes"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-111db0457c3b","stem":"About symptoms of chagas disesase","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chagoma refers to unilateral peri-orbital swelling with conjunctivitis"},{"label":"B","text":"Patient may present with headache malaise prostration"},{"label":"C","text":"Splenomegaly and hepatomegaly are not common"},{"label":"D","text":"Myocardial damage and gastrointestinal symptoms occurs in early disease"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above are true"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4bf2d8147a68","stem":"About the causative agent of human African sleeping sickness","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"T.b.gambesiense causes acute form of sleeping sickness"},{"label":"B","text":"T.b.gambesiense is transmitted by the riverine morsitans group"},{"label":"C","text":"T.b.gambesiense and T.b.rhodesinse can be distinguished microscopically"},{"label":"D","text":"T.b.rhodesinse is a more virulent form, person to person transmission via tsetse fly is uncommon"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-523a9af35a0f","stem":"About trypanosome brucei sub species life cycle","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Procyclic trpomastigote are infective"},{"label":"B","text":"Procyclic trpomastigote have a variant Antigen coat"},{"label":"C","text":"Two major morphological form exists; trypomastigotes and epimastigotes"},{"label":"D","text":"Stromoxys (stable flies) can cause cyclic transmission. BEST WISHES Page 13 of 13"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c74369055cb0","stem":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?>","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"<a:clrMap xmlns:a=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main\" bg1=\"lt1\" tx1=\"dk1\" bg2=\"lt2\" tx2=\"dk2\" accent1=\"accent1\" accent2=\"accent2\" accent3=\"accent3\" accent4=\"accent4\" accent5=\"accent5\" accent6=\"accent6\" hlink=\"hlink\" folHlink=\"folHlink\"/>"},{"label":"B","text":"*€urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags"},{"label":"C","text":"€place"},{"label":"D","text":"*€urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags"},{"label":"E","text":"€country-region"},{"label":"F","text":"*€urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["duplicate_option_text"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_text","nonunique_option_text","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d345471c620f51033193346114ce04085734c807"},{"id":"q-36b45846735c","stem":"Which metacestode stage can undergo asexual re