 30% lymphocytes 70% monocytes 45% are eosinophil Several Polymorphonuclear leukocytes may be found in a neonatal patient’s CSF The following is not true: In bacterial meningitis PMNs predominate Differential cell count alone can differentiate between bacterial and nonbacterial meningitis In more than 10 % of bacterial meningitis cases will show a lymphocytic predominance Viral, fungal, and tuberculous infections Lymphocytosis predominate Possible consequences of Pachymeningitis are: Extradural abscess Subdural abscess Leptomeningitis All of the above Infectious meningitis is broadly classified into types namely: Acute pyogenic meningitis Acute lymphocytic (viral, aseptic) meningitis Chronic viral meningitis Only A and B are correct The statement is NOT true with regard to acute pyogenic meningitis: CSF becomes turbid or frankly purulent. The turbid fluid is particularly seen in the sulci Pus accumulates in the epidural space The turbid fluid is particularly seen in the base of the brain The most common form of Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia (CAH) results from a deficiency of which of the following?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3abd724ee7bf","stem":"What type of hypersensitivity reaction lies in the base of urticarial pathogenesis?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Immunology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourc